Z||000000||gtsonly||11-22-2000||01:30 PM||||I have an 86 gt V6, since I have owned the car I am experiencing a hesitation on hard throttle. If I apply normal pressure to either the gas pedal or manually move the throttle there is no hesitation but if I am to open the throttle fast I get a hesitation. I have gone through the car over and over. New plugs, wires, cap, rotor, timing right on, no codes, no vaccum leaks and I am at a loss. A friend of mine who has had crisp throttle just started to experience this same thing. Was I able to explain it right? I do not have a crisp throttle. But I would like to say once I got the RPM's up it is fine. Just if you trump it hard off the start it has a hesitation. HELP PLEASE!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-22-2000||03:16 PM||||I'd start by checking the throttle position sensor (TPS).  See if its output voltage varies smoothly and linearly with throttle position. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||strdream||11-22-2000||05:34 PM||||After that, check your fuel pressure.  If I am understanding you right it sounds like a fuel delivery problem.  Check it with a gauge.  It was to be within specs.   The ECM uses the MAP sensor for the amount of fuel to deliver as well as the temp sensors.  Make sure the vac line to the MAP is not restriced.<BR>Ross||||reg||1
